        {
          "id": 3152727121,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "What I noticed during testing (NSIS vs (new) WiX (via CMake/CPack improvements not part of this MR)) is that the installers install different versions of IANA-ITU-ALARM-TC-MIB because the file exists in separate folders from the \"share\" (iana and ietf) and since the Wireshark installation of the SNMP mibs is a flat directory, one is (intentionally or unintentionally) overwritten.\nHow are we supposed to know which one's \"right\"?",
