        {
          "id": 3155908274,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "As stated in #21089, I think we need to start distributing MIBs in the folder structure provided by libsmi.  It looks like Wireshark already has the architecture to support it (supports multiple MIB paths).  I just didn't check if Wireshark defaults to looking it subdirectories or if users would have to individually add all of the new folders.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
