        {
          "id": 3287444375,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I'm pretty sure that Wireshark defaults to looking into subdirectories, because for the Linux packages we don't distribute the MIBs and just rely on the MIBs and folder structure provided by libsmi, because libsmi ends up being a shared library requirement.\n\nThen that plays into a MSYS2 install a little bit - I think for a MSYS2 build the MIBs don't work when running from the build directory but they do work after the package is installed.",
