        {
          "id": 3287583275,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Sorry, that was poorly worded, it doesn't recurse into directories other than possibly via include directives in files themselves. When libsmi is compiled, it sets a default path list and uses directory separators instead of recursing, so we would have to do something similar in `oids.c` to do that (we can't really compile it in, because the installation directory can change.)\n\nlibsmi hasn't had any changes in years. I don't know if the author is accepting patches, or if we'd have to fork it to fix, e.g., #1827.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
